<!--
    GH-8500: "stack address taken, stored, then dereferenced is mis-analysed."
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8500

    Source (gcc -O0):
      int identity(int x) {
        int *p = &x;     // take the address of the (stack-resident) parameter
        *p = x;          // store THROUGH the pointer back into the stack slot
        return *p;        // read THROUGH the pointer
      }

    The address of the parameter's stack slot (s-0x1c) is spilled to another
    stack slot (s-0x8 = `p`).  The value is then stored through `p` (`*p = x`)
    and re-read through `p` (`return *p`).  Resolving the alias requires the
    indirect STORE/LOAD through `p` to be recognized as touching s-0x1c.

    Bug: the store-through-pointer is dropped.  The STORE `*p = x` is converted
    to a stack varnode (s-0x1c = x) and then dead-code-eliminated in the SAME
    main-loop iteration, one step BEFORE the aliasing LOAD `return *p`
    collapses to read s-0x1c.  With the store already gone, the load re-heritages
    s-0x1c with no reaching definition, so it resolves to an *uninitialized*
    stack input.  The rendered C returns an undefined local:

        return xStack_1c;

    Stage model: S6 "alias-facets" / heritage ordering.  The kuna fix is an
    option-gated extension of ActionDeadCode::lastChanceLoad (the existing
    mechanism that already defers dead-store removal for not-yet-resolved
    LOADs whose pointer is an "eventual constant"): when a LOAD dereferences a
    pointer that is itself a value living on the stack (an unresolved
    pointer-to-stack alias), it conservatively holds the stack stores alive for
    that deadcode round, so the store survives until the alias resolves.
    Gated by the default-off arch flag stack_alias_deadstore
    (`option stackalias on`).

    Pass 1 (default pipeline) reproduces the bug: the function returns the
    uninitialized local `xStack_1c` (assert #1).
    Pass 2 (after `option stackalias on`) recovers the store-through-pointer,
    so the function returns the parameter (assert #2): no `xStack_1c` survives.

    Disassembly (identity @ 0x1139):
      1139 55              PUSH RBP
      113a 4889e5          MOV  RBP,RSP
      113d 897dec          MOV  dword ptr [RBP + -0x14],EDI
      1140 488d45ec        LEA  RAX,[RBP + -0x14]
      1144 488945f8        MOV  qword ptr [RBP + -0x8],RAX
      1148 8b55ec          MOV  EDX,dword ptr [RBP + -0x14]
      114b 488b45f8        MOV  RAX,qword ptr [RBP + -0x8]
      114f 8910            MOV  dword ptr [RAX],EDX
      1151 488b45f8        MOV  RAX,qword ptr [RBP + -0x8]
      1155 8b00            MOV  EAX,dword ptr [RAX]
      1157 5d              POP  RBP
      1158 c3              RET
-->
